    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (17 tests, 0 failures/errors), including the new `Cp09Tests`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `customerCode` needed to be **stored** (the test reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, not from the create response) and computed at creation time. I followed the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern per `AGENTS.md`:\n\n1. **`Owner` model** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `customerCode` field with `@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`, plus getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `customer_code VARCHAR(20)` to the `owners` table in all four schemas (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, postgres, mysql for consistency).\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct's `toOwnerDto` auto-maps it into the response.\n\n4. **New function** `AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2014 reads the built `Owner` via `@Val`, computes `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` where `LAST3` is the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` and `NNNN` is `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` zero-padded to 4 digits, and sets it on the entity.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted an `assignCustomerCode` step (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `build` and `save`, so the count reflects owners *before* the new one is persisted.\n\nPlacing the step before `save` makes the sequence \"one more than the current number of owners\": owner A gets `N+1`, then after A is saved owner B sees `N+1` owners and gets `N+2` \u2014 exactly the `+1` relationship the test asserts (`SMI-\u2026` then `JON-\u2026` with consecutive sequence numbers).",
